Time for a few new item ideas:
(1) Sunglasses (just kidding)

(2) A building trowel, like you use for making brick walls.
    It would do the opposite of a pickaxe, letting you make walls,
    or smooth out a bunch of corridor spaces into a finished floor
    to make a room with.

(3) Levels with just one or two small rooms, letting you dig your
    own level.  You'd probably want a magic pick axe (blessed?)
    that let you dig automatically when you moved, like dwarves do.

(4) The option to retire (for those who are bored with traveling
    through mazes).  When retiring, your current dungeon level is stored as
    a bones level, the room you are in is reduced to having only
    one door, and your character becomes a shop keeper, and any
    stuff on the floor becomes available for sale.

